# The haggle: name, apple origin, shelf life, price, a discount on one (refused), five (granted).
# speaker | what the speaker sets out to do (their goal; they word it themselves)
elf | You are at Mara's fruit stall in the town market with the warrior, buying fruit for the road north. Greet her warmly and ask Mara, as a question to her, name, in your own words.
elf | Pick up an apple and ask Mara, as a question to her, where her apples come from.
warrior | Step in gruffly: ask if the apples will survive a week on the road.
elf | Ask Mara, as a question to her, how much one apple costs.
elf | Ask Mara, as a question to her, for a discount on just that one apple.
warrior | Grumble that you are not made of coin; one apple at that price is robbery.
elf | Offer to buy five apples instead and ask for a discount on the five.
elf | Ask Mara, as a question to her, what the five apples will cost with her discount.
warrior | Grunt that five is fine and you will carry the sack; ask her to pack them.
elf | Thank her and ask once more for her name so you can find the stall again.
